// EDID golden tests. The four blocks are the binary EDIDs that the `edid` crate
// (0.3.0, `testdata/`) uses for its own tests, copied byte for byte. The expected
// values were decoded independently in Python from the same bytes (offsets as in
// the Linux kernel's `struct edid`) and agree with the crate's expectations
// where it states them (vendor, product, serial, week, year, video input, size,
// gamma, the first timing, the name and serial descriptors).
module bleu::ddc::edid_test;
import std::core::mem, std::time, bleu::error, bleu::ddc::edid;

